---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import SafetyDemo from '../components/khensu/SafetyDemo.astro';
import FramePass from '../components/khensu/FramePass.astro';
import StatStrip from '../components/khensu/StatStrip.astro';

interface Props {
  ogCard?: string;
  canonicalUrl?: string;
  title?: string;
  description?: string;
  scroll?: string;
}

const {
  ogCard = 'safety',
  canonicalUrl,
  title = 'The violet flame',
  description = 'The violet flame is the transmuting fire of Lumeria. Each frame is checked on your device, and nudity, gore or an attack is blurred before you see it. First offense: a 1 month ban from the public forum.',
  scroll,
} = Astro.props;
---

<Base
  title={title}
  description={description}
  ogCard={ogCard}
  canonicalUrl={canonicalUrl}
>
  <section class="page-head" data-hero>
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">the violet flame · nu.network</p>
      <h1><span class="aura-text">The violet flame.</span><br /><span class="dim">Covered before you see it.</span></h1>
      <StatStrip
        items={[
          { n: 0, label: 'Copies of a flagged picture sent to us, or to Apple, to make the warning' },
          { n: 1, unit: 'month', label: 'First offense. Banned from the public forum' },
        ]}
      >
        The violet flame. Each frame is checked on this device. A clear frame plays. Nudity, gore or an attack is blurred before you see it.
        The first offense bans them from the public forum for a month.
      </StatStrip>
      <p class="lede">
        The violet flame is the transmuting fire of Lumeria. Priests and priestesses of the sacred fire used it in the
        temples: discord went into the flame, and the energy came back as light. Human rights and creators come first.
        A clear frame plays. Nudity, gore, or an attack on people for who they are, hits the flame on your device and
        blurs before you see it. The public forum bans them.
      </p>
      <SafetyDemo />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="safety-nudity">
    <div class="wrap">
    <div class="split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">nudity</p>
        <h2><span class="aura-text">Blurred before you see it.</span><br /><span class="dim">On this device.</span></h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          <a href="https://support.apple.com/en-us/105071">Sensitive Content Warning</a> helps you avoid an unwanted
          sensitive photo or video. If a photo or video might contain nudity or gore and violence, it is blurred before
          you view it. You choose Show, or you look at the resources and block.
        </p>
        <p>
          The check is Apple’s Sensitive Content Analysis. It runs on your device. On a live stream, each frame goes
          through the video-stream analyzer before it is shown, including on the host’s preview. A clear frame plays.
          When the analyzer finds nudity, or gore and violence, that frame blurs immediately, before you see it. The
          frames before it stay clear. Apple does not receive a detection, and does not get the frame. Neither do we.
        </p>
        <p>
          Gore and violence detection is on iOS 27, iPadOS 27 and macOS 27. A child account follows Communication
          Safety. The app respects the setting in Privacy &amp; Security. Teen accounts from Declared Age Range get
          sensitive images blurred, and no messages from strangers.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <FramePass />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="safety-hate">
    <div class="wrap split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">hate speech</p>
        <h2><span class="aura-text">An attack on people</span><br /><span class="dim">for who they are.</span></h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          Hate speech is an attack on a person or a group for who they are. Race, colour, ethnic or national origin,
          sex, gender, sexual orientation, religion, disability and age are covered. Apple’s warning does not cover
          words, so this check runs beside it, on the device.
        </p>
        <p>
          If a guest says it in the middle of a stream, the picture blurs and the sound drops at that moment, until you
          tap Show. The warning names the kind of attack. It does not quote the words.
        </p>
        <p>
          The host sees the same cover on their own preview, so they know a guest tripped it. Show and Block are your
          choice on this device. The public forum ban is the account, and it is instant.
        </p>
        <p>
          A list you subscribe to, from a community or a newsroom, can hide more. A label informs. It does not delete
          the post. Nudity, gore, and an attack on people for who they are ban the person from the public forum.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="safety-rule">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">the violet flame</p>
      <h2><span class="aura-text">Human rights and creators first.</span><br /><span class="dim">We are no-nonsense.</span></h2>
      <div class="prose rule">
        <p>
          Creation and play can happen on some other toxic platforms. We are no-nonsense. We prioritize the high vibe
          of the community over racism, misogyny, bullying, and just random drama dumb-fuckery.
        </p>
        <p>
          Three strikes, then a year. The first offense is an instant ban from the public forum for 1 month. The
          second is 3 months. The third is 6 months. While the ban lasts they are blocked from the public forum, and
          they lose nu.waves, except the sound healing tones, First Attempt, and the classical composers.
        </p>
        <p>
          The fourth offense bans them from public discourse for 1 year. The fifth is permanent: that person, that
          wallet, and that device are banned from public discourse. The count never resets, even years later.
        </p>
      </div>
      <ol class="ladder">
        <li><b>1</b><span>1st offense<br />1 month</span></li>
        <li><b>3</b><span>2nd<br />3 months</span></li>
        <li><b>6</b><span>3rd<br />6 months</span></li>
        <li><b>1 year</b><span>4th<br />public discourse</span></li>
        <li><b>permanent</b><span>5th<br />you, your wallet, your device</span></li>
      </ol>
      <p class="fine">
        Private messages stay private. The frame never leaves the device. The post stays on the network. Stock apps do
        not show that person in public discourse until the ban ends. A permanent ban does not end. Money already in the
        wallet stays spendable.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="safety-facts">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">facts</p>
      <h2><span class="aura-text">A label sits on the post.</span><br /><span class="dim">The post stays.</span></h2>
      <div class="grid three">
        <article class="glass">
          <h3 class="aura-text">Your lists</h3>
          <p>Anyone can publish a label list. Newsrooms, fact-checkers and communities already do. You subscribe to the ones you want, and ignore the rest.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="glass">
          <h3 class="aura-text">Where people disagree</h3>
          <p>A consensus label is shown only when raters who usually disagree agree on it. Every device computes the same label. The ratings are public.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="glass">
          <h3 class="aura-text">What a label can say</h3>
          <p>Factual, with sources. Opinion. Misleading. Fraud or scam. Spam. Adult. Graphic violence. Satire. Made with AI. A label informs. It does not delete.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="safety-exception">
    <div class="wrap split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">the narrow exception</p>
        <h2><span class="aura-text">One thing is not speech.</span></h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          Child sexual abuse material, and other content illegal everywhere, is refused by hash. Node operators do not
          cache those addresses. The app does not show them. The list is public, append-only and limited to that
          content, so it cannot quietly become a political filter.
        </p>
        <p>
          <a href="/security">Security</a> is how the messages stay unreadable.
          <a href="/feed">The feed</a> is where a post meets this cover.
          <a href="https://media.khensu.nu">nu.media</a> is the clip under the warning.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
    </section>
    {scroll && (
      <script is:inline define:vars={{ scroll }}>
        const go = () => document.getElementById(scroll)?.scrollIntoView({ block: 'start' });
        if (document.readyState === 'complete') go();
        else window.addEventListener('load', go);
      </script>
    )}
</Base>

<style>
  .dim {
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.5);
  }
  .page-head .lede {
    margin: clamp(1.6rem, 4vw, 2.4rem) 0 0;
    max-width: 46rem;
  }
  h2 {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }
  .split {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.9fr) minmax(0, 1.2fr);
    gap: clamp(1.5rem, 5vw, 4rem);
    align-items: start;
  }
  .prose p {
    color: var(--text-dim);
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
  }
  .prose p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }
  .glass {
    padding: 1.3rem 1.4rem;
    border-radius: 22px;
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.04);
    border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.11);
    box-shadow: inset 0 1px 0 rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);
  }
  .glass h3 {
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  .glass p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--text-dim);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }
  .grid.three {
    margin-top: 1.6rem;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 260px), 1fr));
  }
  .rule {
    max-width: 46rem;
    margin-top: 1.4rem;
  }
  .rule p {
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.78);
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    line-height: 1.45;
  }
  .ladder {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(5, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 0.7rem;
    margin: 1.6rem 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }
  .ladder li {
    padding: 1rem 0.8rem 0.9rem;
    border-radius: 18px;
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.04);
    border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.11);
  }
  .ladder li:nth-child(n + 4) b {
    font-size: clamp(1.15rem, 2vw, 1.65rem);
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
  }
  .ladder b {
    display: block;
    color: #fff;
    font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 3vw, 2.6rem);
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.04em;
    line-height: 1;
  }
  .ladder span {
    display: block;
    margin-top: 0.45rem;
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.55);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }
  .fine {
    margin: 1rem 0 0;
    max-width: 68ch;
    color: var(--text-dim);
    font-size: 0.92rem;
  }
  @media (max-width: 800px) {
    .split {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 1.2rem;
    }
    .ladder {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }
  }
  @media (max-width: 420px) {
    .ladder {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }
  }
</style>
